{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle passes through the three vertices of an isosceles triangle that has two sides of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a base of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. What is the area of this circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/9/bc9d8b9f630c6970845b712342467cbba9955cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 2\\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{5}{2}\\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{81}{32}\\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 3\\pi \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\frac{7}{2}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"429\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> have vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, with foot of altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> intersecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd6654d76ebcb5aa78bf644545d9639c8fccd53a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; pair B=(0,0), C=(2,0), A=(1,3), D=(1,0); pair O=circumcenter(A,B,C); draw(A--B--C--A--D); draw(B--O--C); draw(circumcircle(A,B,C)); dot(O); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,O,W); label(&quot;\\(r\\)&quot;,(O+A)/2,SE); label(&quot;\\(r\\)&quot;,(O+B)/2,N); label(&quot;\\(h\\)&quot;,(O+D)/2,SE); label(&quot;\\(3\\)&quot;,(A+B)/2,NW); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(B+D)/2,N); [/asy]\" width=\"232\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>Then by the Pythagorean Theorem (with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d008b0f638eecc580a199181c4bf3895784e726b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OD = h$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />) on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/5/e75efb6abaae407233baf1ad552792b2982c9757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e225bbbd6e79777bba07d4043109ece480d93a19.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} h^2 + 1 &amp; = r^2 \\\\ (h + r)^2 + 1 &amp; = 9 \\end{align*}\" width=\"132\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Substituting and solving gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a556d411a92237862585d419bf21a5691e694c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac {9}{4\\sqrt {2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"68\" height=\"42\" />. Then the area of the circle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/3/45343bca549eeb70cac8804857cab611f84c1351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2 \\pi = \\left(\\frac {9}{4\\sqrt {2}}\\right)^2 \\pi = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac {81}{32} \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"238\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>By <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24ad33198cbeac568be32a33ad27d05575e38c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac {1}{2}Bh = \\frac {abc}{4R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"128\" height=\"38\" /> (or we could use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a91bbfd0ed8dd526d21ec9b36cc90c3f951a5103.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Heron%27s_formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Heron&#39;s formula\">Heron's formula</a>),\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/6/3e633da80f20d181d823e5f1ae8ba9d76bad76fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = \\frac {abc}{2Bh} = \\frac {3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 2}{2(2)(2\\sqrt {2})} = \\frac {9}{4\\sqrt {2}}\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"43\" />\nand the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7dadc25488e10d48133f9982103e5c793868985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R^2 \\pi = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac {81}{32} \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"134\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Alternatively, by the Extended <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Sines\" title=\"Law of Sines\">Law of Sines</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/c/e8c9e4437a60d324994ccf3463f040abe8b58da6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2R = \\frac {AC}{\\sin \\angle ABC} = \\frac {3}{\\frac {2\\sqrt {2}}{3}} \\Longrightarrow R = \\frac {9}{4\\sqrt {2}}\\]\" width=\"301\" height=\"47\" />\nAnswer follows as above.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Extend segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/0/7609b3287774915ebf4e80694297138491851a07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; pair B=(0,0), C=(2,0), A=(1,3), D=(1,0), R=(1,-0.35); pair O=circumcenter(A,B,C); draw(A--B--C--A--D--R--C); draw(B--O--C); draw(circumcircle(A,B,C)); dot(O); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,S); label(&quot;\\(O\\)&quot;,O,W); label(&quot;\\(R\\)&quot;,R,S); label(&quot;\\(r\\)&quot;,(O+A)/2,SE); label(&quot;\\(r\\)&quot;,(O+R)/2,SE); label(&quot;\\(3\\)&quot;,(A+C)/2,NE); label(&quot;\\(1\\)&quot;,(C+D)/2,N); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>By the Pythagorean Theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/b/20bae5e12d2632fb54993e56b145e80866960791.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD^2 = 3^2 - 1^2\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf855c574c47d4adfe02415b542ec78c2305dcef.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD = 2\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8eabc87afe4c11a47e4aa27628d5517af4866b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb5f81e8a4268637ec8f6cfeafffdbee5528060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACR$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/b/2bb09cda9a14a319ee298f85108d1ccea8cb440a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {2\\sqrt{2}}{3} = \\frac {3}{2r}\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"41\" /> which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068ce0a056a24d56aaa2274b6a69d7e43d211949.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r = \\frac {9}{2\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac {9\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\]\" width=\"139\" height=\"45\" /> therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/9/6c965d62373a67169e4b33da037d9346e9d3ee72.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac {9\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>The area of the circle is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/04250010557d0f1e76a6233cfe9b97291eb5d8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2 = \\left(\\frac {9\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\right)^2 \\pi = \\boxed{\\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac {81}{32} \\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"240\" height=\"56\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First, we extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to intersect the circle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710fb5fa3adedd7a16739e543d846747adbe05b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/315635f0b6afac6eba65f160b4765f8a089b242a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; pair B=(0,0), C=(2,0), A=(1,3), D=(1,0), E=(1,-(8^0.5)/8); pair O=circumcenter(A,B,C); draw(A--B--C--A--E); draw(circumcircle(A,B,C)); dot(O); dot(D); dot(B); dot(C); dot(A); dot(E); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$O$&quot;,O,W); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(A+B)/2,NW); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(B+D)/2,N); [/asy]\" width=\"208\" height=\"252\" /></center>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, we know that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/4/184993d354c51ec846b92ab7db734408bd7415c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1^2+AD^2=3^2\\implies AD=2\\sqrt{2}.\\]\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" />\nWe also know that, from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Power_of_a_Point_Theorem\" title=\"Power of a Point Theorem\">Power of a Point Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df46c997de5643a2353c4ab9296ac2a4308d7af4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AD\\cdot DE=BD\\cdot DC.\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" /> \nWe can substitute the values we know to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed0635c1f7848d211d69de36918ec6a5ced3e2f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot DE=1\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />\nWe can simplify this to get that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/9/c19312c2cd0459963595b99319c399fad66547f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DE=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{8}.\\]\" width=\"94\" height=\"41\" />\nWe add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> together to get the length of the diameter, and then we can find the area.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/e/71ea1512510ba3cbcf0d77d0acf358f4bf87e702.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AE=AD+DE=2\\sqrt{2}+\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{2}}{8}=\\dfrac{9\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"41\" />\nTherefore, the radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fe258ed3bf0cdba0d2396b5b906308c53b40cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9\\sqrt{2}}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />, so the area is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f9d02075e4cc213c3fb5f56002933b9a1b1871e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left(\\dfrac{9\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\right)^2\\pi=\\boxed{(\\text{C})\\dfrac{81}{32}\\pi.}\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"56\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Another possible solution is to plot the circle and triangle on a graph with the circle having center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. \nLet the radius of the circle = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \nLet the distance between the origin and the base of triangle = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b06371a9052a4f43086e040471c8b28fe4e6a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 + a^2 = r^2\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb9965ccfd8130f05bb6033e814d3a4a08a0d5b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r + a = 2\\sqrt{2}\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ccbf8e73d27c08dcb264c65b7e5b45fd57f1ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 2\\sqrt{2} - r\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511ac67b6010544f85b1dbbcd52c78b0e4a45ef5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9 - 4r\\sqrt{2} = 0\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953da2d9a76fd4c334a729e3a993df7cf7ba1e2a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r = \\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\]\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/829a87e608cc795c1c9ab3bc2bad6c6eec088a24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi r^2 = \\boxed{(\\text{C})\\frac{81}{32}\\pi}\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can also use LOC to solve this problem. If O is the center of the circle, angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/14323858397d132fc0169507e1fb72c5ae7ef54d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is double angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edcdc0d73ef64ec441f60a3a8dccdbd10aa61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. From law of cosines, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d420e194093e786fc5d37f30520ba030415eccc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos(\\angle BAC) = \\frac{7}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"38\" />. We now apply law of cosines on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/14323858397d132fc0169507e1fb72c5ae7ef54d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OBC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/1/a11af5bf8eb8c2f697252bda707607f0b11b3e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 = r^2+r^2-2r^2\\cos(2 \\angle BAC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"243\" height=\"21\" /> but we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da5c5a40f3e30ab15b0e8e0ea59cd4732dba34a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cos (\\angle BAC) = 2 \\cdot (\\frac{7}{9})^2 - 1 = \\frac{17}{81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"267\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging this in and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55fe2b0c7476d1f4fb6ce4cb4b60b7a63c465058.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{9}{8} \\cdot \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"85\" height=\"38\" /> and thus the area of the circle is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd2414afec532275a8bdae0cc0b1d7ba4f096316.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{81}{32} \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"35\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B\">2007 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\